# Build-time (Vite) environment for the FoodOS.ai site.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables reach the browser bundle, and everything here
# IS PUBLIC by design — it ends up in the shipped JavaScript. Never put a
# secret in a VITE_ variable.
#
# In CI these are set as GitHub Actions **repository variables** (not secrets)
# and passed to `vite build`. See docs/runbooks/website-setup.md (DevOps).

# The Google Apps Script web app `/exec` URL that receives demo requests
# (apps-script/, FOO-7). Deployed by the CTO; paste the URL the deploy dialog
# gives you, including the /exec suffix.
#
# Leave it empty and the form shows an inline "Demo booking isn't configured
# yet" state instead of submitting — a fresh clone runs with no setup.
VITE_DEMO_REQUEST_URL=""


# --- Build configuration (NOT shipped to the browser) -------------------------
# These two have no VITE_ prefix on purpose: vite.config.ts reads them, and
# Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to the bundle. They decide where
# the site thinks it lives. Both have working defaults; set them only to build
# for a different URL.

# Vite's `base` — the path the site is served from.
#   /foodos.ai/   GitHub Pages project site (the default, and what CI builds)
#   /             a custom domain, once foodos.ai points at Pages
# Get this wrong and every asset 404s: the page loads blank. `npm run
# check:dist` fails the build rather than letting that ship.
# BASE_PATH="/foodos.ai/"

# The origin the absolute URLs in robots.txt and sitemap.xml are built from.
# Switch to https://foodos.ai at the same time as BASE_PATH="/".
# SITE_ORIGIN="https://doylefermi-kv.github.io"
